# PART 10: The Masked Ball of Monsieur - A Kiss, A Challenge, and Three Rapiers
# ==============================================================================
PARTS_06_TO_10[10] = [
    "In the winter of sixteen hundred and ninety-five, one of the most glamorous and talked-about social events of the Grand Siècle took place: the Grand Royal Masked Ball hosted by Monsieur, Philippe I, Duke of Orléans, the King's brother, at the Palais-Royal. The grand ballrooms were transformed into an enchanted wonderland of mirrored galleries, thousands of glittering wax candles, and cascading garlands of winter greenery and silver ribbons that shimmered in the ambient light.",
    "Julie arrived at the masquerade dressed in the height of male aristocratic fashion: an exquisite coat of midnight-blue velvet embroidered with silver thread, silk breeches, lace cravat, and a stylish black velvet carnival mask. Moving through the glittering assembly of masked courtiers, princes, and duchesses with effortless swagger and noble poise, she was widely admired as one of the most handsome and charming young cavaliers at the ball.",
    "During the festivities, Julie became enchanted by a beautiful young noblewoman who was dancing in the central gallery. Approaching the lady with gallant charm and witty conversation, Julie danced with her through several graceful minuets. As the dance concluded near a flower-draped alcove, Julie boldly and tenderly kissed the young marquise on the lips, creating a sensational moment of delightful audacity that was witnessed by several watching courtiers.",
    "Three young aristocratic suitors, who had each been competing for the lady's favors, were deeply offended by what they perceived as an intolerable insult from an unknown young cavalier. Confronting Julie as she stepped out into the palace courtyard, the three noblemen demanded immediate satisfaction, challenging the mysterious youth to an instant duel of honor outside the palace walls.",
    "With cool, amused serenity, Julie accepted their challenge without hesitation. Rather than retreating or revealing her female identity to avoid combat, she invited all three gentlemen to follow her into the secluded gardens behind the Palais-Royal, where the snowy lawns and trimmed hedges lay quiet beneath the crisp, starlit winter sky of Paris.",
    "In the moonlit garden clearing, with the distant music of the palace violins drifting softly through the frozen air, Julie faced the first challenger. Saluting politely with her rapier, she engaged him with lightning speed. Within minutes, her flawless technique disarmed the nobleman, leaving him nursing a minor puncture wound in his sword arm as he looked on in disbelief.",
    "Without pausing to rest, Julie turned to the second challenger. Her footwork on the packed snow was immaculate, maintaining perfect balance as she parried his aggressive lunges and swiftly ran her blade through his sleeve, disarming him with effortless precision. The third nobleman, stepping forward with grim determination, met the same swift fate, his sword sent spinning into the snowy bushes by Julie's masterly circular bind.",
    "Having defeated all three noblemen in consecutive duels in less than a quarter of an hour without suffering a single scratch, Julie politely wiped her blade with her lace handkerchief, sheathed her rapier, and bowed with immaculate courtly courtesy. Leaving the three astonished and humbled gentlemen in the garden, she casually strolled back into the warm ballroom to finish her champagne and resume dancing.",
    "The news of the extraordinary triple duel spread like wildfire through the ballroom. When the court discovered that the dashing cavalier who had defeated three of the best swordsmen in the royal guard was none other than the prima donna Mademoiselle de Maupin, the ball erupted into a mix of shock, laughter, and immense admiration. Julie's legendary feat became the sensation of Paris overnight.",
    "However, dueling was strictly forbidden throughout France by the severe edicts of King Louis XIV, carrying the penalty of imprisonment or death. Recognizing that the three wounded noblemen would be forced to report the incident to the King's marshals, Julie quietly slipped away from the palace into the snowy night, seeking temporary refuge outside the capital while her friends petitioned the King for royal mercy."
]

